{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1558536866,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NDcxODUxMDI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3449","origin":"github"},"title":"run: Should a warning be issued when actual outputs do not match specified?","message":"A complement to #3448 (globbing outputs post run): if user does specify some `--output`s but at the end we save more or completely different set of files, we have a \"dichotomy\" between expected and actual outputs.  Any later analysis of the \"graph\" would come to the same question -- should we take only the specified by user outputs, or factual ones, or the union? (may be user specified outputs were re-generated and just didn't differ from previous state).  \nIn `--explicit` mode only the user-specified outputs are saved, so it becomes an intersection of action + specified. In non`--explicit` mode I think it would be useful to forewarn (and ultimately allow to adjust/amend somehow) that specified `--output`s were not sufficient or were completely different.  For that to work re-globing of outputs should be done after run (thus relation to #3448)","files":null}]}